  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 1}{t}^{2})\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 1}t)\\,j+({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t)\\,k \\\\  & =({1}^{2})\\,i+1\\,j+\\operatorname{ln}\u20611\\,k \\\\  & =1\\,i+1\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =i+j, \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) & =({lim}_{t\\to 1}\\frac{3}{t})\\,i+({lim}_{t\\to 1}(4-t))\\,j-({lim}_{t\\to 1}({t}^{2}-1))\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}\\,i+(4-1)\\,j-({1}^{2}-1)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i+3\\,j-0\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i+3\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 1}[4f(t)-g(t)] & =4{lim}_{t\\to 1}f(t)-{lim}_{t\\to 1}g(t) \\\\  & =4(i+j)-(3\\,i+3\\,j) \\\\  & =i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$",
